{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And your strength shall be spent in vain.</b> A man who did not labor, did not plow, did not sow, did not hoe, did not prune, did not herd — and at harvest time blight comes and strips it — there is nothing in that. But a man who labored and plowed and sowed and hoed and pruned and herded, and blight comes and strips it — his teeth are set on edge." "<b>And your land shall not give its produce.</b> Even what you bring to it at sowing time (Sifra)." "<b>And the tree of the land.</b> Even from the earth it shall be stricken — that it does not set its fruit at the setting time (ibid.)." "<b>Shall not give.</b> It governs both above and below — tree and fruit." "<b>Shall not give its fruit.</b> When it does fruit it drops its fruits — there are two curses, and there are here seven punishments (Sifra)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:43.052357772Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}